WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.769
In 1957, two astronomers in Mexico
photographed a faint blue dot.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:09.302
They gave it a number, six hundred and
eighteen, and moved on.

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:13.429
Years later, astronomers realised what
they had actually found.

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:16.633
One of the brightest objects in the
universe.

00:00:16.993 --> 00:00:20.939
And at its centre, the heaviest black hole
ever weighed.

00:00:21.299 --> 00:00:23.763
Nothing should be able to grow that big.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:25.063
Not that early.

00:00:25.423 --> 00:00:26.450
Not that fast.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.302
Relay, this is Jonah.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.449
I can see it.

00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:34.416
Even from here, it's blinding.

00:00:35.126 --> 00:00:36.316
We see you, Jonah.

00:00:36.676 --> 00:00:37.544
Take it slow.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.112
We're right behind you.

00:00:39.822 --> 00:00:42.129
These are the recordings they sent back.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:49.409
TON 618 is so far away that its light left
it ten point eight billion years ago.

00:00:49.769 --> 00:00:53.452
Earth is only about four and a half
billion years old.

00:00:53.812 --> 00:00:56.381
The light we see from it is older than our
planet.

00:00:56.741 --> 00:01:01.427
When that light set out, the universe was
only about three billion years old.

00:01:01.787 --> 00:01:07.809
And already, this black hole weighed
somewhere between forty and sixty-six

00:01:07.809 --> 00:01:08.867
billion Suns.

00:01:09.227 --> 00:01:10.726
That's the mystery.

00:01:11.086 --> 00:01:12.504
There shouldn't have been enough time.

00:01:13.214 --> 00:01:16.090
Iris, my instruments can't even fit the
numbers.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.036
What is this thing?

00:01:19.536 --> 00:01:23.401
Iris, the disk is brighter than anything
I've ever seen.

00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:25.159
I can't look straight at it.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:27.882
TON 618 is a quasar.

00:01:28.242 --> 00:01:33.292
Gas spiralling into the black hole forms a
disk that heats up and shines so brightly

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:36.298
that it drowns out the light of its entire
galaxy.

00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:42.245
That's why two astronomers could see it at
all, from ten billion light years away.

00:01:42.955 --> 00:01:44.860
Your hull temperature is climbing.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.921
Pull back from the disk, Jonah.

00:01:47.631 --> 00:01:48.821
Pulling back.

00:01:49.181 --> 00:01:50.955
Going over the top of it instead.

00:01:52.455 --> 00:01:53.967
Now the black hole itself.

00:01:54.327 --> 00:01:59.573
Its event horizon, the point of no return,
measures about two thousand six hundred

00:01:59.573 --> 00:02:04.244
times the distance from the Earth to the
Sun, from one side to the other.

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:09.684
You could fit every planet in our solar
system inside it more than forty times

00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:10.010
over.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:14.315
Our own galaxy's black hole weighs about
four million Suns.

00:02:14.675 --> 00:02:18.496
TON 618 is at least ten thousand times
heavier.

00:02:19.206 --> 00:02:21.487
It doesn't look like an object anymore.

00:02:21.847 --> 00:02:23.836
It looks like a hole in the universe.

00:02:25.336 --> 00:02:26.759
I'm going closer.

00:02:27.119 --> 00:02:30.857
Iris, everyone says this is where you get
torn apart.

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:34.212
For a small black hole, that's true.

00:02:34.572 --> 00:02:39.298
Its gravity changes so sharply that your
feet are pulled far harder than your head,

00:02:39.298 --> 00:02:42.828
and you'd be stretched apart before you
ever reached the edge.

00:02:43.188 --> 00:02:46.212
Scientists really call it
spaghettification.

00:02:46.572 --> 00:02:50.365
But TON 618 is so enormous that its
gravity changes gently.

00:02:50.725 --> 00:02:56.319
At the edge, the stretch across a human
body is far too small to feel.

00:02:57.029 --> 00:02:58.601
I don't feel anything.

00:02:58.961 --> 00:02:59.879
Nothing at all.

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:02.335
That's the scariest part.

00:03:03.045 --> 00:03:06.105
Close to the edge, the light behaves even
stranger.

00:03:06.465 --> 00:03:11.291
The black hole bends light from behind it
up and over the top, so you can see parts

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.268
of the disk that should be hidden.

00:03:13.978 --> 00:03:16.656
Iris, the sky is folding.

00:03:17.016 --> 00:03:20.681
I can see the back of the disk, bent over
the top of the black hole.

00:03:22.181 --> 00:03:23.785
Jonah, you're at the limit.

00:03:24.145 --> 00:03:26.555
If you cross, there is no coming back.

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:29.027
Not even light comes back from there.

00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:30.439
I know.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:33.140
But someone has to see what's on the other
side.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.193
Tell everyone the blue dot was worth it.

00:03:36.903 --> 00:03:40.519
Crossing the event horizon, Jonah feels
nothing special.

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:42.598
No wall, no flash.

00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:45.511
For him, time keeps running normally.

00:03:45.871 --> 00:03:49.242
But nothing he sends can ever reach us
again.

00:03:49.602 --> 00:03:55.727
And at TON 618's size, he would have at
most about twelve days before reaching the

00:03:55.727 --> 00:03:56.250
centre.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.334
I watched him the whole time.

00:04:00.044 --> 00:04:03.610
From the outside, the story looks
completely different.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.498
Iris never sees Jonah cross.

00:04:06.858 --> 00:04:12.744
His image turns redder, his signal arrives
slower and slower, and he grows dimmer and

00:04:12.744 --> 00:04:13.229
dimmer.

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:15.024
He just stopped.

00:04:15.384 --> 00:04:17.402
Frozen, right at the edge.

00:04:17.762 --> 00:04:19.087
And then he faded away.

00:04:19.797 --> 00:04:23.548
To the rest of the universe, Jonah never
falls in.

00:04:23.908 --> 00:04:27.377
He is still there, at the edge, fading
forever.

00:04:28.877 --> 00:04:32.510
So how did TON 618 get so big, so early?

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:34.554
We still don't know for certain.

00:04:34.914 --> 00:04:40.895
But in 2023, NASA's Chandra and Webb
telescopes found a black hole that seems

00:04:40.895 --> 00:04:42.681
to have been born huge.

00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:47.470
Not from a dying star, but from the direct
collapse of a giant cloud of gas, just

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.641
four hundred and seventy million years
after the Big Bang.

00:04:51.001 --> 00:04:56.042
If giants like TON 618 got a head start
like that, the mystery of the blue dot may

00:04:56.042 --> 00:04:57.456
finally have an answer.

00:04:58.956 --> 00:05:00.950
Jonah's journey was imagined.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.893
The blue dot was not.

00:05:03.253 --> 00:05:08.659
In 1957, two astronomers wrote down number
six hundred and eighteen, with no idea

00:05:08.659 --> 00:05:10.795
they had photographed a monster.

00:05:11.155 --> 00:05:14.985
Every fact about TON 618 in this story is
real.

00:05:15.345 --> 00:05:19.746
If you want to fall into another world
with us, subscribe.
